description:
Design a combinational circuit that computes the factorial of a 4-bit input number (ranging from 0 to 15). For each possible input value, the module produces the corresponding factorial as a 32-bit output. If the input number is outside the defined range, it outputs zero. This implementation utilizes a case statement to map specific input values directly to their precomputed factorial results.
module top_module(
    input [15:0] num,
    output reg [31:0] fact
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [15:0] num,
    output reg [31:0] fact
);always @(*) begin
    case(num)
        0: fact = 1;
        1: fact = 1;
        2: fact = 2;
        3: fact = 6;
        4: fact = 24;
        5: fact = 120;
        6: fact = 720;
        7: fact = 5040;
        8: fact = 40320;
        9: fact = 362880;
        10: fact = 3628800;
        11: fact = 39916800;
        12: fact = 479001600;
        13: fact = 1932053504;
        14: fact = 1278945280;
        15: fact = 2004310016;
        default: fact = 0;
    endcase
end

endmodule

