description:
Design a 16-bit to 32-bit sign extension circuit. The module takes a 16-bit input and extends it to 32 bits by replicating the sign bit (the most significant bit) of the input to fill the upper bits of the output. This allows for the correct representation of negative numbers when widening the bit width of signed integers.
module top_module(
		imme, out
    );

code:
module top_module(
		imme, out
    );parameter IMME_SIZE = 16;
	parameter DATA_SIZE = 32;

	input wire [IMME_SIZE-1:0] imme;
	output wire [DATA_SIZE-1:0] out;

	assign out = {{(DATA_SIZE-IMME_SIZE){imme[IMME_SIZE-1]}}, imme};

endmodule

