description:
Design a sign magnitude converter that transforms a 12-bit linear encoded signed representation into its appropriate output based on the sign input. If the sign input is high (1), the module computes the two's complement of the input value (inverting the bits and adding one) to represent a negative number in a 12-bit format, except for a specific case where the input equals negative maximum (-4096), which outputs the positive maximum (2047). If the sign input is low (0), it simply passes the linear encoded value to the output.
module top_module(

  linear_enc_sign, sign,

  conv_sig
  );

