Design a 4-bit binary counter with synchronous reset functionality. On each rising edge of the clock, when the reset signal is active, the counter resets to zero; otherwise, it increments its value by one. The counter maintains its value using two registers, where one holds the current count and the other captures the previous count for synchronizing the increment operation.
