Implement a one-bit full adder circuit. It takes three inputs: two binary numbers (a and b) and a carry-in (cin). The module outputs the sum (s) and a carry-out (c). The sum is calculated by XORing the inputs, and the carry-out is determined through a combination of AND and OR operations among the inputs, reflecting the standard behavior of a full adder in digital logic.
